{"name":"Pistachio Dream","hex":"#a5cf8c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pistachio","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deciduous tree (Pistacia vera) grown in parts of Asia for its drupaceous fruit.","The nutlike fruit of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pistachio"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pistachio","blocks":[{"text":"The pistachio is a small to medium-sized tree of the cashew family. The tree produces seeds that are widely consumed as food. Pistachios can be used as an ingredient in desserts, chocolate, candy, ice cream, and as a paste or butter. As a tree nut, pistachios are considered a priority allergen that may induce allergic reactions in susceptible people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Pistachio_vera.jpg/330px-Pistachio_vera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pistachio","wikidata":"Q36071"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse","wikidata":"Q105563495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg/500px-860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg/1280px-860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg/500px-860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pistachios growing in Iran in 2007. The fruits have not yet begun to open.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A860631-Pistachio-IMG_6862-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Feuilles_de_pistachier.jpg/500px-Feuilles_de_pistachier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Feuilles_de_pistachier.jpg/1280px-Feuilles_de_pistachier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Feuilles_de_pistachier.jpg/500px-Feuilles_de_pistachier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Leaves of the pistachio tree","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFeuilles_de_pistachier.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Dormant_Pistachios_in_